<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hispania Citerior</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/197-bce">197</a>–<a href="/years/27-bce">27 BCE</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/2nd-century-bce">2nd century BCE</a> · Also known as Nearer Spain</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hispania">Hispania</a> Citerior, &quot;Nearer <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>&quot;, was the Roman province created in 197 BCE from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>'s conquests along the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a> coast of eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iberia">Iberia</a> after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-punic-war">Second Punic War</a>. Its governors extended Roman rule inland through the Celtiberian and Lusitanian wars. Augustus reorganised it as the much larger province of Hispania Tarraconensis, governed from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tarraco">Tarraco</a>.</p></div>
